@inherits LayoutComponentBase
@implements IDisposable
@inject NavigationManager Nav
@inject IConciergeStateService State

@*
    The shell is a frame and nothing else.

    It used to carry a top bar with a brand and a ⋯ menu, and then a five-tab
    bottom navigation bar. Neither reference has either: Codex has a sidebar,
    Claude Design has modes. Concierge is one workspace now, and the workspace
    draws its own sidebar — so the only thing left for a layout to do is hold
    the page.

    The permission prompt used to live here, above everything, as a modal. It
    has moved into the thread: a run stops in the middle of doing something,
    and covering the work to ask about it hides the context the answer depends
    on. It is now the last thing in the conversation, which is where the run
    actually stopped.
*@

@Body

<div id="blazor-error-ui" data-nosnippet>
    Something went wrong.
    <a href="." class="reload">Reload</a>
    <span class="dismiss">×</span>
</div>

@code {
    // The shell watches nothing itself any more; the workspace reads the
    // services it needs. IDisposable is kept because the host registers the
    // layout as disposable and removing it is a separate change.
    public void Dispose()
    {
    }
}
